{"name":"Lucky Dog","hex":"#d3c8ba","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lucky dog","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone with astounding good luck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky_dog"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Lucky Dog","blocks":[{"text":"The Lucky Dog (1921) is the first film to include Stan Laurel and Oliver Hardy together in a film before they became the famous comedy duo of Laurel and Hardy. Although they appear in scenes together, Laurel and Hardy play independently. Laurel is the star as the hero of the film and Hardy plays the main villain opposite him."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/L%26H_Lucky_Dog_1919.jpg/330px-L%26H_Lucky_Dog_1919.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lucky_Dog","wikidata":"Q1815435"},{"title":"Lucky Dog (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucky Dog is a 1933 American drama film directed by Zion Myers and written by Zion Myers and Roland Asher. The film stars Charles \"Chic\" Sale, Tom O'Brien, Harry Holman and Clarence Geldart. The film was released on April 20, 1933, by Universal Pictures."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Dog_(film)","wikidata":"Q22000697"},{"title":"Lucky Dog (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucky Dog by Leo Butler is a play which premiered in the upstairs Jerwood Theatre of Royal Court in 2004. It was directed by James Macdonald, and featured Linda Bassett and Alan Williams in the lead roles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1f/LuckyDogcover.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Dog_(play)","wikidata":"Q6697885"},{"title":"Dog","blocks":[{"text":"The dog is a domesticated descendant of wolves. Also called the domestic dog, it was selectively bred during the Late Pleistocene by hunter-gatherers. Dogs and the modern gray wolf share a common ancestor. Dogs were the first species to be domesticated over 14,000 years ago, before the development of agriculture, though genetic studies suggest the domestication process may have begun over 25,000 years ago. Due to their long association with humans, dogs have gained the ability to thrive on a starch-rich diet that would be inadequate for other canids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Huskiesatrest.jpg/330px-Huskiesatrest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dog","wikidata":"Q144"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg/500px-Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg/1280px-Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg/500px-Laurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lobby card with (from left) Stan Laurel, Oliver Hardy, and Jack Lloyd","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaurel_and_Hardy_in_Lucky_Dog.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_merle_koolie_short_coat_heading_sheep_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_me